{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786438114,"nonce":"Pi/dm+EHLfKqqU/v6VD4q3/OhM0=","message":"Done. **11 test files, 136 tests, all passing**; `tsc --noEmit` exits 0. `--passWithNoTests` removed from both `test` and `verify` in web/package.json, so the ui job can no longer go green by finding nothing.\n\n**The FilterBar failures were two real defects, not bad test queries.**\n\n1. `ToggleGroup` (components/ui/primitives.tsx) rendered a `\u003cfieldset\u003e` (implicit role=group, named by its `\u003clegend\u003e`) wrapping a `\u003cdiv role=\"group\" aria-label={legend}\u003e` — two nested groups with the IDENTICAL accessible name. Assistive tech announced 'Lifecycle state, group' twice and 'the group called Severity' was ambiguous by construction. Fixed the component; the queries were right.\n\n2. ⚠️ THE BIG ONE — a harness bug that had silently disarmed the whole suite. `web/vite.config.ts` inlined solid-js and @solidjs/* for the test transform but NOT @tanstack/solid-query, so solid-query resolved its own copy of Solid. A query resolving after mount updated a store the component's tracking scope never subscribed to: the fetch completed, the data arrived, and `\u003cShow when={clusters.data}\u003e` never flipped. **Every async-query assertion in the suite could only ever have asserted the loading shape.** Fixed by inlining @tanstack/solid-query, with the failure mode written down.\n\n**A live instance of this issue's own example bug, found and fixed.** PoliciesSection.tsx's SUPPRESSED_REASON was typed `Record\u003cstring, string\u003e` and had LOST `snoozed` — 8 contract values, 7 present. The dry run rendered 'Would not send — snoozed.', a wire token where a sentence belongs, on the one panel whose job is explaining a silence. Its sibling DeliveryPanel.tsx holds the same map correctly typed and does include it — the two disagreed. Now typed against the generated `NotificationSuppressedReason` so the next addition is a build failure.\n\nAdded: Actions.test.tsx (12), SnoozeDialog.test.tsx (13), PoliciesSection.test.tsx (4), settings-contract.test.tsx (5), plus src/test/contract.ts helpers that read bounds out of the generated valibot schemas and throw BY NAME if the shape changes, so a valibot upgrade fails loudly instead of returning undefined and making assertions vacuous.\n\nThe ack/snooze rollback assertions are written the way that makes a lie observable: the alert renders OUT OF THE QUERY CACHE, so on a 500 the bar must still offer Acknowledge and never Withdraw acknowledgement, and the detail must not be refetched as though something changed. Settings screens are mounted over DELIBERATELY SHIFTED bounds, proving the screen follows the server rather than merely happening to agree with it.\n\nSSE was already covered and nothing was missing — Last-Event-ID resume (including a sessionStorage resume point surviving reload and a corrupt one being ignored), out-of-order frames not rewinding the resume point, duplicates delivered rather than deduplicated, unknown kinds delivered while still advancing lastSeq, unreadable frames, split chunks, and clean-EOF-as-disconnection.\n\nRemaining hand-copied server truth is filed separately — the largest is that PoliciesSection's priority input has no min/max at all while the contract says 0-10000, and the draft is never piped through CreatePolicyRequestSchema.","files":null}]}